course: dictionary
lesson: 2846
title: One word, two jobs: document
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A document is a piece of writing that matters, often because it is official. As a noun, it can be a paper or a computer file with important writing, such as a passport, letter or report. «A CV is a short, honest document about your skills, results and work.»
explain: Document can also be a verb. To document something means to record it carefully in writing, photos or video. «The Nanjing massacre of 1937–1938 is widely documented» means many careful records of it have been made.
explain: Use the words around it to find the meaning. «Save the document» tells you it is a computer file. «A will is a document in which a person says who should get their things» tells you it is an official paper. Check your choice by putting your meaning into the sentence.
fact: A document is a piece of official or important writing, on paper or on a computer.
fact: As a noun, «document» can mean a passport, a letter, a report or a file on a computer.
fact: As a verb, «document» means to record something carefully in writing, photos or video.
fact: «Identity documents» are papers that show who a person is.
fact: Words can change their job in a sentence. Look for a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action) to see which one you have.
exercise: «Save the document before you close the computer.» What kind of document is this? | A type of cake | A sunny day at the beach | A dog's bed | *A computer file you write
exercise: «A CV is a short, honest document about your skills, results and work.» What is a CV? | *A short document about your skills and work | A long story about a holiday | A bag for school books | A kind of passport
exercise: Mia wants to document her science results. What should she do? | Hide them under her bed | Sing them to her class | *Record them carefully in writing, photos or video | Throw them away
test: «Anna Yaroslavna became Queen of France in 1051; a document survives with her signature.» What is the document here? | A wandering singer | A song sung by kobzars | *A piece of official writing that has survived | A type of crown
test: Which word is a verb in «Historians have documented that many kobzars were persecuted»? | Persecuted | *Documented | Historians | Kobzars
exam: Which sentence uses document as a noun? | «We are documenting the results today.» | «She will document the experiment with photos.» | «The children documented their walk in a diary.» | *«Your passport is an important document, so keep it safe.»
